        {
          "title": "Same index, fairer mix",
          "text": "We still deliver a +3% weighted list increase (\u20ac173,041 on \u20ac5,768,025). The engine does not invent a bigger bill \u2014 it changes which lines carry it."
        },
        {
          "title": "Defend lines are not loaded like captive",
          "text": "Where genuine capture is already lost and street is above market, the engine cuts or holds (e.g. IUK brake pads/rotors). A flat +3% would have raised those the same as captive filters."
        },
        {
          "title": "Blind weight is still partly the old world",
          "text": "23.8% of basket \u20ac still takes the unbenchmarked base lift (NO_EVIDENCE_HOLD, ~6.1% weighted). Differentiation is real where evidence exists \u2014 honest about where it does not."
        },
        {
          "title": "Street on the right point",
          "text": "Street comparisons use PR00 \u00d7 1.785 (street factor), not raw list \u2014 correcting the Eucon-era misread. No oem_benchmark without enough priced peer OEs."
        },
        {
          "title": "New models need mix, not only +3%",
          "text": "D-Max 2.2 (15k oil interval) is a \u03b8 / launch-book story: protect interval-linked wear with mix rules; do not claim volume from the list move alone."
        }
      ],
